MERGE (n:R2G:`Symbol` {id: "sym:tests/test_eval_hardening.py::test_hard_negative_distractor_disambiguation"}) SET n += {`id`: "sym:tests/test_eval_hardening.py::test_hard_negative_distractor_disambiguation", `name`: "test_hard_negative_distractor_disambiguation", `qualname`: "test_hard_negative_distractor_disambiguation", `kind`: "function", `path`: "tests/test_eval_hardening.py", `lang`: "python", `start_line`: 39, `end_line`: 91, `signature`: "def test_hard_negative_distractor_disambiguation(tmp_path: Path):", `docstring`: "Verify that graph structure disambiguates a target from a lexical distractor.\n\n    Scenario:\n    - Entry point `sym:app::handle_request` calls `sym:app::StreamingAdapter` in `adapters.py`.\n    - Distractor `sym:app::Response` in `models.py` has high lexical overlap ('stream', 'adapter', 'response').\n    - BM25 alone ranks the distractor high.\n    - Graph expansion from `handle_request` reaches `StreamingAdapter` via CALLS edge,\n      disambiguating the target and admitting it into context.", `entrypoint`: true};
